index 59a547e10..df80a4f24 100644
--- a/docs/ROADMAP.md
+++ b/docs/ROADMAP.md
@@ -1,5 +1,21 @@
 # My Roadmap

+- [ ] Under #976 I distinguish module-owned generic union declarations with equal source names. My generic-union parameter audit loads two modules that each export Box<T>; both C frontends reject the second declaration as already defined, before checking whether a generic call combines distinct owners. I require independent module loading, same-owner alias compatibility, cross-owner refusal and both producer/native execution. My retained reproducer is in evidence/generic-union-parameters-20261011/owners.
+
+- [ ] Under #976 I preserve selected-variant scalar provenance in C AOT. My Choice<T,E> generic function returns a bool fallback for Left(string), but translation attributes that string payload to the unreachable Right(bool) return and rejects it. Both producers reproduce the same error. I require per-arm finite scalar facts, retained runtime guards, wrong-payload refusals and full translator regressions.
+
+- [ ] Under #976 I reject incompatible generic union call results in unused C-checked bodies. Once concrete union binding works, my negative audit accepts assigning identity(Box<int>.None) to Box<string>. I require complete declaration and instance comparison at local, return, assignment and argument boundaries before code generation.
+
+- [ ] Under #976 I retain specialized union match and native declaration metadata. My expanded generic-union audit emits Box<T> match temporaries for Box<int> parameters, omits concrete union typedefs used only in specialized signatures, and emits a qualified alias with a dot in its C type name. I require complete specialized body and imported declaration execution.
+
+- [ ] Under #976 I lower nested ordinary generic union values through both NanoISA producers. My generic-parameter audit executes Box<int> through the fresh self-hosted compiler but rejects Box<Box<int>> as an unsupported local type. I require retained nested instance metadata, checked selected payloads and VM/C AOT execution; the existing native selected-pattern coverage does not establish NanoISA parity.
+
+- [ ] Under #976 I preserve concrete generic union parameters in C checking. My fresh `unbox(Box<T>,T)->T` probe executes through the self-hosted compiler but both C frontends reject explicit Box<int> and Box<string> arguments as inconsistent generic bindings. I require complete nominal arguments, repeated-variable refusal and executed scalar/nested/callback payloads.
+
+- [ ] Under #976 I admit checked concrete union identities during C NanoISA generic specialization. My `identity(T)->T` probe accepts Box<int> in native and self-hosted compilation, but NanoVirt refuses the parameter identity while compiling mandatory shadows. I require exact union instance metadata and VM/C AOT execution without relaxing incompatible-instance checks.
+
+- [ ] Under #976 I substitute generic union constructors in native specialized bodies. My `box(T)->Box<T>` probe executes through both NanoISA producers, but native emission returns nl_Box_T from a function declared to return nl_Box_int and initializes its generic pointer field from int. I require concrete constructor/result/body identities, multiple instantiations and native execution.
+
 - [x] Under #976 I preserve established enum/int and byte-storage compatibility while validating array mutations. My full compiler audit rejects nine parser operations that append ParseNodeType enum values to array<int>; I require the existing scalar conversion contract alongside exact callable signatures, with parser self-compilation and byte narrowing controls. My [final functional callback evidence](evidence/selfhost-functional-callbacks-20261010/README.md) records eleven paired methods, eleven native-product methods, adjacent scalar/union checks, the full translator gate and unchanged eleven-stage compiler self-compilation.

 - [x] Under #976 I retain complete self-hosted for-loop binding types. My refreshed functional-array audit finds that returning a callable loop binding is rejected as int; both the previous native compiler and the current seed preserve the prior artifact on this valid-source refusal. I require callable binding, returned value and incompatible indirect-call checks across named/computed/inline/empty loops. I retain the paired failure in [my functional callback evidence](evidence/selfhost-functional-callbacks-20261010/loop-product-baseline.json); this remains separate from the corrected map/filter/reduce implementation. My [final functional callback evidence](evidence/selfhost-functional-callbacks-20261010/README.md) records eleven paired methods, eleven native-product methods, adjacent scalar/union checks, the full translator gate and unchanged eleven-stage compiler self-compilation.
